From f4024b931bf76bdc26e0e3d73575692b859ab7f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: cedrus: jpeg: enable on H616, fix tables, limits
 and queue setup

Fixes and additions to the JPEG decoder for the H616 (and the others):

- Enable it on the H616, and set the rotate/scale output enable and
  MC no-writeback bits in the MPEG control register there, as the
  vendor library does on this IC.
- Map the source buffer into the kernel for JPEG: the header parser
  read through vb2_plane_vaddr(), which is NULL with the queue's
  DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING. Requests stay mandatory for every codec
  except JPEG instead of being dropped for all of them.
- Grey (one component, written with chroma format 4:0:0) and 4:1:1
  pictures, beside 4:2:0, 4:2:2, 4:2:2 transposed and 4:4:4. Anything
  but 4:2:0 is written as 4:2:0. For grey pictures the chroma plane is
  filled with neutral values.
- Rewrite the Huffman upload as one byte stream laid out as the SRAM
  image, and use the T.81 annex K tables for missing DHT tables
  (Motion-JPEG from webcams has none).
- Range-check the scan's Huffman selectors (an out of bounds read
  before) and the quantisation table selectors; reject 16-bit tables
  rather than truncating them.
- Reject what the engine cannot decode, since it holds one luma and one
  chroma table set: Cr tables different from Cb, non-interleaved scans
  and scan component orders that differ from the frame.
- Check that the picture and its MCU padding fit the capture buffer
  instead of capping at 2048x2048, and program the 16-bit MCU count
  fields. The VLD end address is the last byte of the source buffer.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
